  "note": "Fort emplacement: a snappable poured-concrete gun-platform revetment. Built-in ImageGen reskin of templates/fort-emplacement-guide.png (fort-emplacement-guide.py); exact prompt retained beside this file (fort-emplacement.prompt.txt), raw retained unmodified. 1536x1024 RGBA. ImageGen did not hold the 192px pitch: the nine patch frames are one contiguous 3x3 picture cut at 181px squares from (22,11), and the three platform variants are 212px squares - the document's rects are authoritative, not the 8x4 grid. Block fort.emplacement (wall-3x3, slots read 'the exterior is on this side'): raised parapet along the exterior, flat platform inside; the centre slot is platform. Platform variants are doodads. Presentation art only - cover and topology belong to the post/pad that stamps it. New sheet, shares no id with a shipped tileset.",
